<p>President Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping held more than two hours of talks at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing on Thursday, during the first visit to China by a U.S. president in nearly nine years. The leaders exchanged public praise, attended a state banquet and discussed trade, Iran, the Strait of Hormuz and Taiwan. Trump invited Xi and his wife, Peng Liyuan, to visit the White House on Sept. 24. China’s post-meeting statement placed Taiwan at the center of the bilateral relationship and warned that mishandling it could lead to “clashes and even conflicts.” A White House account provided to reporters did not mention Taiwan, instead citing talks on keeping the Strait of Hormuz open, Chinese purchases of U.S. agricultural products and ending flows of fentanyl precursors. The White House said Trump and Xi agreed that the Strait of Hormuz “must remain open to support the free flow of energy,” while Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Washington wanted Beijing to play a more active role in pressing Iran over Gulf tensions. Trump told reporters before the trip that he did not think the United States needed China’s help with Iran, saying, “We’ll win it one way or the other, peacefully or otherwise”.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/kQADp-fCNMZcjrdL2I9sg8gsgLxvEXdEQPeTSFSOKrPT12pmYWlGLq4tvv8ZwF7KTgYnUZQBmjl0hY_L-Z7QckM1MavjavublRo1IdPgB2-hIYOQ19MxA8qN4N9pU1YuLeT0OOQRXtQN2UCGk9xa9K2C0yBD02UpPC30E6mmLTkVyJf5mObU4corAaHXChhDNSejRSXv5wyregcgrFnVrLIcvPQhhPgdZODqh260RNaXNTio_iuiKfO0xM5xKkD13Ep3N-QQewzGeGItHw' alt='China&#x27;s President Xi Jinping and U.S. President Donald Trump pose for a photo at the Temple of Heaven in Beijing on May 14, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Optics: Handshakes, arm taps and frequent asides between Xi and Trump drew attention during the visit, according to SCMP.</li><li>Business delegation: Trump traveled with executives including Elon Musk, Tim Cook and Nvidia’s Jensen Huang, and SCMP reported the business delegation’s combined personal net worth exceeded $1 trillion.</li><li>Relationship framework: The leaders agreed to describe ties as a “constructive, strategically stable relationship,” with cooperation and “measured competition” as the stated frame.</li><li>Security concerns: U.S. allies worried Trump could disavow U.S. support for Taiwan, perhaps inadvertently, during the summit.</li></ul><blockquote>The Taiwan question is the most important issue in China-US relations - Xi Jinping</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Chinese government: Chinese officials said pre-summit trade talks produced “generally balanced and positive outcomes,” while still treating political disputes as limits on the broader relationship. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/plus/news/china/diplomacy/article/3353545/xi-trump-summit-casts-optimistic-light-lingering-tensions'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>White House: The White House described the meeting as a good one and said the sides discussed ways to enhance economic cooperation. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-invites-chinese-president-xi-jinping-for-september-24-visit-at-white-house/article70978383.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Secretary of State Marco Rubio: Rubio said instability around the Strait of Hormuz threatens Asian economies that rely heavily on the waterway, and that Beijing had its own interest in preventing escalation. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-xi-talks-us-to-persuade-china-to-play-more-active-role-in-resolving-iran-war-crisis-says-marco-rubio/article70976894.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Chinese President Xi Jinping: Xi said the relationship affects not only the 1.7 billion people in China and the United States but also the roughly 8 billion people outside the two countries. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/make-it-work-and-never-mess-it-up-xi-jinping-tells-donald-trump-at-beijing-summit-11495150#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><